<p>A court in Russia&#x27;s Kursk region sentenced former Governor Alexei Smirnov to 14 years in a maximum-security prison and fined him 400 million rubles after finding him guilty of taking bribes linked to contracts for fortifications on the border with Ukraine. Prosecutors said Smirnov took bribes from companies hired to build the border defenses. Bloomberg described the case as defrauding the government through the embezzlement of public funds meant for those fortifications.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Financial penalty: Alongside the prison term, the court fined Smirnov 400 million rubles, highlighting the scale of the corruption case described by the regional court&#x27;s press service.</li><li>Border contracts: The case centered on firms hired to build fortifications along the Russia-Ukraine border, tying the prosecution directly to wartime defense spending.</li><li>Regional focus: A court in Kursk Oblast, the border region whose defensive preparations were at the heart of the case, handed down the sentence.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kursk regional court: The court&#x27;s press service said the prosecution ended with a 14-year sentence and a 400 million ruble fine for Smirnov. (<a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/06/former-russian-governor-gets-14-year-prison-sentence-for-taking-bribes-tied-to-border-fortifications'>Meduza</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera&#x27;s reporting: Al Jazeera framed the verdict around allegations that Smirnov took bribes from companies hired to build border fortifications, emphasizing the link between corruption and regional defense works. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/6/russia-jails-former-kursk-governor-in-ukraine-incursion-linked-graft-probe'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Bloomberg&#x27;s reporting: Bloomberg described the case as defrauding the government by embezzling public funds intended for fortifications along the Russia-Ukraine border, highlighting the state-finance side of the prosecution. (<a href='https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-04-06/ex-head-of-russia-s-kursk-region-gets-14-years-in-jail-for-graft'>Bloomberg</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/6/russia-jails-former-kursk-governor-in-ukraine-incursion-linked-graft-probe'>Russia jails former Kursk governor in Ukraine incursion-linked graft probe</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/06/former-russian-governor-gets-14-year-prison-sentence-for-taking-bribes-tied-to-border-fortifications'>Former Russian governor gets 14-year prison sentence for taking bribes tied to border fortifications</a> - meduza.io</li><li><a href='https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-04-06/ex-head-of-russia-s-kursk-region-gets-14-years-in-jail-for-graft'>A court in Kursk Oblast, Russia, sentences former governor Alexei Smirnov to 14 years in prison for defrauding the government by embezzling public funds intended for building fortifications along the Russia–Ukraine border.</a> - bloomberg.com</li></ul>